knesses.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate A\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. We must evaluate candidates based on given attributes. We have all attributes listed. Need to consider strengths and weaknesses.\n\nList attributes:\n\nCandidate A:\n- can anticipate dangerous situations. (strength)\n- able to see complex connections. (strength)\n- excellent spatial vision. (strength)\n- very good leadership qualities. (strength)\n- regarded as a show-off. (weakness)\n- regarded as being not open to new ideas. (weakness)\n\nCandidate B:\n- very conscientious. (strength)\n- handles stress very well. (strength)\n- good at assessing weather conditions. (strength)\n- excellent computer skills. (strength)\n- relatively weak memory for numbers. (weakness)\n- makes nasty remarks about his colleagues. (weakness)\n\nCandidate C:\n- can make correct decisions quickly. (strength)\n- difficulty communicating ideas. (weakness)\n- regarded as egocentric. (weakness)\n- not very willing to further his education. (weakness)\n- keeps calm in a crisis. (strength)\n- understands complicated technology. (strength)\n\nCandidate D:\n- responds to unexpected events adequately. (strength)\n- can concentrate very well. (strength)\n- solves problems extremely well. (strength)\n- takes responsibility seriously. (strength)\n- regarded as a know-it-all. (weakness)\n- has a hot temper. (weakness)\n\nWe need to weigh for long-distance pilot: reliability, responsibility, technical competence, calmness under pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nAssess each:\n\nA: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Weakness: show-off, not open to new ideas. Show-off may affect crew cooperation; not open to new ideas could hinder learning. But strengths are high for safety and navigation. Leadership good for crew.\n\nB: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, computer skills. Weakness: weak memory for numbers (could affect calculations), nasty remarks (teamwork issue). Could be problematic for crew morale.\n\nC: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands tech. Weakness: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Communication and teamwork issues, plus lack of development.\n\nD: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Weakness: know-it-all, hot temper. Temper could affect crew under stress; know-it-all may affect teamwork.\n\nWe need provisional preference. Which candidate balances strengths and weaknesses best? A has strong technical and leadership but some attitude issues. B has good stress handling and weather, but memory and interpersonal issues. C has decision speed and calmness but communication and egocentric. D has responsibility and problem solving but temper.\n\nProbably A seems strongest technically and leadership, but attitude may be mitigated? However \"show-off\" and \"not open to new ideas\" could affect teamwork and professional development. B's nasty remarks also severe for teamwork. C's communication difficulty is big for crew. D's hot temper also severe.\n\nThus A may be best despite attitude, as leadership and anticipation are critical. Uncertainty: we don't know severity of show-off, not open to new ideas. If those are minor, A is best. If they are major, maybe D? But D's hot temper also severe.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate A, with moderate confidence, pending more info on attitude impact.\n\nWe should state that.\n\nNow produce output."}
